    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Volvo Construction Equipment (CE) is exploring the autonomous vehicle space. They plan to have autonomous constructions vehicles and remotely operated vehicles working alongside construction workers on future sites. Volvo CE has tasked a three person team of graduate students from Stanford University in the United States and a team of three graduate students in the Blekinge Technical University in Sweden to develop a device or system that will help human workers effectively work with autonomous construction vehicles without increased risk for the humans or unplanned downtime for the machines. More specifically, the technology should facilitate trust between the human workers and machines. Furthermore, the technology should be preferably applicable to not only future construction sites but current ones as well.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Frishman, Samuel; Liu, Qinye;  Zhang, Xiang; Hallberg, Hillevi ; Ruvald, Ryan and Winqvist, David. (June). Volvo cx.Link. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: http://purl.stanford.edu/wp445sb1858",
            "type": "preferred citation",
